Simon Tatham <anakin@pobox.com> writes:
>I generally find it's sufficient to never let them into the level
>I'm currently solving. Leave them by the stairs, go up into level 1,
>solve level 1, go down and get them. Then leave them on level 1
>while solving level 2, and bring them up to help you out with the
>roomful of stuff at the end.
>This technique generally seems to keep them tame, out of the way,
>and yet still have them around when I need them most.

I used to occasionally find that my pet would go feral in the
time taken to do the top two levels, particularly if you get
bogged down taking out lots of monsters hiding behind boulders
when you can easily lose track of just how long you are taking.

So now I make a point of going back down to them at least a
couple of times while solving each level, even if I'm certain
they are well fed.

Actually, my favoured strategy is to bring a chest to the bottom
of the sokoban stairs and bring all the loot down to it as
I go, which works quite nicely with keeping your pet alive
and tame in the above manner.

